<p>Seeking Greenlights:** Yes.</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article</p>
<p>Genre: Horror</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> Janual Grey is a mixed-race of a human and a Lovecraftian-horror. He's identified to be a powerful reality-altering eldritch abomination.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>After receiving witness reports from a family, claiming that while they were in the middle of driving on the mountain highways to visit a family member, the car had some issues, and they've accidentally crashed through the guardrails and are now half-way to their death. They were trying to find a way to safely get out of the car when one of them noticed that something behind the car is approaching them, when it arrives it moved the car back on the road before spontaneously disappeared. As the person who witnessed its appearances, the youngest daughter, said that she saw a monster that saved them. When this was brought to the Foundation. They knew they have an anomaly on the chase. The location of its presence is identified to be somewhere near the woods of Acadia National Park. Soon, an MTF was dispatched to detained the SCP after an unexpected confrontation.</p>
<p>Based on some of the Foundation's logs, the SCP's real name is &quot;Janual Grey&quot;. It is a powerful-reality bending anomaly capable of causing out disturbances to a large fraction of reality.</p>
<p>The main issue here: after a few testings were made to demonstrate his powers, the Foundation is currently discussing whether to use him as an asset in terminations of other hostile SCPs that pose a great threat to the Foundation and the entire world or continue to study more of his capabilities.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The Foundation needs to learn more of his potentials, origins, and relationship connected to the cult and the so-called &quot;Darkness&quot;.</p>

							</div>

								
