<p>So I am not seeing the comedy, what about this is funny to you?</p>
<p>ALSO I don't see why he has to eat people of any sort, why can't he consume normal food? Sorry, but cannibalism is a very boring trope to express horror. I personally find it occurs with such regularity I just don't know why people still use it. It just screams &quot;edgy&quot;</p>
<p>The idea that he is consuming prisoners in an effort to avoid hurting &quot;innocent&quot; people is a rather disgusting perspective, as if maybe those prisoners don't deserve to be alive as much as innocent people?</p>
<p>Also, this thing is a cannibal, I don't see him as much of a &quot;kind hearted joe&quot; where do you intend to expand this? One can't just say someone is kind hearted, one needs to write how that is going to be communicated to the reader.</p>
<p>More importantly, I don't see any story here. You repeat yourself a few times, wasting words you could be using to explain what story you're going for.</p>

